A||||6||billfredmike24||Trim question when painting||||1||
Z||000000||billfredmike24||08-20-2001||12:07 PM||||I'm getting my car painted in the near future and was wondering how to move the trim?  Am i gonna break most of it? Will i need new trim or just clips?  What's the best way to move it?  Also can i paint the trim on the back fascia as it's all faded and what should i use to do it?<BR>Thanks MIke||||reg||1
Z||000001||jch82||08-20-2001||12:47 PM||||You will have to get new clips. Some of them are held in place with screws as well.<P>As for painting, you can just buy some black paint. Wetsand the moldings so the paint will stick and spray them. If you want, you could also go over the moldings afterwards with a can of clearcoat...<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mom and Dad they quite don't understand it<BR>ALl the kids they laugh as if they planned it<BR>Why do girls wanna pierce their nose <BR>And walk around in torn pantyhose, oh yeah<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-20-2001||12:57 PM||||some of them like on the door have screws at end, then you sorta push the molding down toward the ground then pry the bottom out with a thin screwdriver or putty knife. then it just lifts off. If the plastic clips are old some will snap off. there not very expensive for new. You can paint the moldings, recommend the SEM molding paint from auto body paint store. You can get the right shade from flat to gloss black. Its made to adhere to plastic better than just old spray paint. Sand them with scotchbrite or coarse steel wool first.||||reg||1
Z||000003||XDrewX||08-20-2001||03:36 PM||||I have noticed some people have just painted over the molding, I will be getting my car painted eventually, and I have really been having a hard time deciding to get the molding painted the same as the car.  <P>I am sooooo afraid the molding will start to flake and chip and crack.<P>How has everyones molding held up who has had it painted ??? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ditz88GT||08-20-2001||03:41 PM||||I painted mine the same color as the body, and it's holding up great!<P><P>------------------<BR>~Ditz88GT<P>E-mail: cditzler@hotmail.com<BR>AIM: Ditz88GT<BR>http://go.to/fiero||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||08-20-2001||03:44 PM||||I Didn't have my trim painted with the rest of the body- and it Looks OK...but It would've been nicer if the trim had at least been painted black- the original color is starting to fade and looks more gray than black sometimes.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
